==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Komuso Cat''' at Level 10.

Evolves into '''Brass Cat''' when obtained from [[Symphony of Bankruptcy (Merciless)|Symphony of Bankruptcy]] (guaranteed to drop) and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
Pied Piper Cat is essentially an Aku-specific [[Onmyoji Cat (Rare Cat)|Thaumaturge Cat]], meaning that his use in that matter is heavily replaceable. Along with that, his horrendous survivability makes him quite hard to stack. Pied Piper Cat's only advantage over Thaumaturge Cat is shorter foreswing, and even this advantage means little when considering that Pied Piper Cat doesn't even have 100% uptime on his [[Weaken]]. Additionally, as many Aku enemies are safe behind a [[Shield]], Pied Piper's Weaken chance effectively drops to 40% or depends on another unit to pierce that Shield. Thaumaturge can also gain [[Immune to Waves|Wave Immunity]] through [[Talents]], while Pied Piper isn't even immune to [[Surge Attack|Surges]].

While his decent Shield Piercing capabilities may sound appealing, his terrible health and subpar range make him a bad choice when it comes to that matter. [[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Cat Researcher]], [[Ancient Egg: N109 (Rare Cat)|Barrel Cat]] and [[Ancient Egg: N004 (Special Cat)|Supercar Cat]] simply perform better in all areas. Cat Researcher in particular has similar Shield Piercing chances when you count in time between attacks, but with much better range and attack speed. This unit is still usable against short-ranged Aku enemies such as [[Aku Gory]], but his lack of survivability really takes its toll and makes this unit a lackluster one overall.

In a cruel twist of irony, Pied Piper Cat comes from a [[Aku's Melody (Merciless)|fairly challenging Aku stage]]. Any players who can beat that stage without this underwhelming Cat Unit have barely any need for him.

==='''True Form'''===
The health increase is great on a unit like Brass Cat, who, in prior forms, would lack the HP necessary to survive even one attack from all notable matchups. Its speed is also increased from 7 to 12, allowing it to reach the frontlines slightly faster while also slipping into the blind spots of [[Ackey]]s and other [[:Category:Long Distance Enemies|Long Distance enemies]] easier.

This form also increases its Shield Piercing chance from a 40% to a decent 60%, pairing well with its quick attack rate. Furthermore, it gains a 50% chance to create a level 2 [[Wave Attack|Mini-Wave]], giving it a pseudo-Area Attack as well as extending its effective range to '''532.5'''.

Even with this, the chance of it getting both its Mini-Wave as well as Shield Pierce off in the same attack remains a measly 30%, which means most of the time the Mini-Wave will either only carry the weaken effect, or the Shield Piercing will be on a single enemy. Additionally, Brass Cat remains very much vulnerable to the Aku enemies it's supposed to target, as it doesn't gain Surge Immunity to deal with the Surges many of them can create and is frail in comparison to Barrel Cat while lacking the range of Cat Researcher.

Despite these inconsistencies, Brass Cat proves to be a decent True Form, improving this cat's usage greatly.

